WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Welcome to the show,
Congressman.

00:00:01.368 --> 00:00:02.669 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
Thanks for having me.

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:03.503 line:92%
-I want to ask about you this,

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:04.704 align:start size:94% position:6%
which must have been
a trippy night

00:00:04.704 --> 00:00:07.007 line:92%
for you when you won election.

00:00:07.007 --> 00:00:09.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was 2016.
That was election night.

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:11.811 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was.
-So a big night for you.

00:00:11.811 --> 00:00:13.279 line:92%
And yet a weird night overall.

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:16.816 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I had lost two election
before then.

00:00:16.816 --> 00:00:18.084 size:84% position:42% line:92%
And as my brother says,

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:21.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
2016 was the year
anyone could get elected.

00:00:21.421 --> 00:00:22.022 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:22.022 --> 00:00:25.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's a very nice way
of a brother...

00:00:25.325 --> 00:00:28.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So I made it.
-...for a brother to say.

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:29.729 align:start size:94% position:6%
I want to move on
to some other stuff.

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:33.099 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I have to ask, like,
what has it been like for yo

00:00:33.099 --> 00:00:35.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
this week with
the impeachment hearings?

00:00:35.135 --> 00:00:38.038 align:start size:94% position:6%
Has it changed your take
on any of it?

00:00:38.038 --> 00:00:39.706 size:81% position:41% line:92%
And are you surprised?

00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:40.774 line:92%
Or is it what you expected

00:00:40.774 --> 00:00:43.109
that it doesn't seem like it's
changed any Republican minds

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:46.079 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, that it hasn't.
But this is not complicated.

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:48.314
I mean, you can sum up the whole
thing in one sentence.

00:00:48.314 --> 00:00:51.051 size:81% position:41%
Donald Trump pressured
the Ukraine president

00:00:51.051 --> 00:00:53.787 align:start size:94% position:6%
to dig up dirt on Joe Bide
and withheld aid.

00:00:53.787 --> 00:00:56.589 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you got hours and hour
and hours of testimony.

00:00:56.589 --> 00:00:58.058 line:92%
But there's no factual dispute

00:00:58.058 --> 00:00:59.893 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, we ought
to vote to impeach.

00:00:59.893 --> 00:01:02.195 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There you go.
That was very simple.

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:04.531 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:04.531 --> 00:01:08.101
-And the Republicans, they don't
have a factual defense.

00:01:08.101 --> 00:01:08.902 size:81% position:41% line:92%
So they basically say,

00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:10.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Okay, let's just attack
the witnesses."

00:01:10.937 --> 00:01:14.107
It's like if your team is
losing, down 20 points,

00:01:14.107 --> 00:01:15.075 line:92%
you just attack the refs.

00:01:15.075 --> 00:01:17.143 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, that's basically
their strategy.

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:19.279 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think Washington
Congressional hearings

00:01:19.279 --> 00:01:21.247 align:start size:94% position:6%
is always remarkable because
you know,

00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:23.683 size:88% position:44%
you see people elected
from across the country.

00:01:23.683 --> 00:01:26.219
And some of them are good
at talking to witnesses.

00:01:26.219 --> 00:01:28.822
Some of them are not good
at talking to witnesses.

00:01:28.822 --> 00:01:30.657 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-You represent Silicon Valley.

00:01:30.657 --> 00:01:34.160 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think one thing that i
always notable to me

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:38.031 align:start size:94% position:6%
is how often,
when Congress people

00:01:38.031 --> 00:01:38.965 line:92%
are interviewing tech leaders,

00:01:38.965 --> 00:01:42.869
they don't seem to understan
how even the Internet works.

00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:44.037 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:44.037 --> 00:01:45.038 line:92%
-Well, the technology hearings

00:01:45.038 --> 00:01:47.373 align:start size:94% position:6%
haven't been one of
the finer moments in Congress.

00:01:47.373 --> 00:01:49.409 size:81% position:41%
And there are a lot of
embarrassing moments.

00:01:49.409 --> 00:01:52.712 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, you know,
when you have senators asking,

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:54.347 line:92%
"How does Facebook make money?

00:01:54.347 --> 00:01:56.216
Or you had one member of
Congress, he literally --

00:01:56.216 --> 00:02:00.253
he held up his iPhone and he
starts yelling at Google C.E.O.,

00:02:00.253 --> 00:02:02.722 align:start size:94% position:6%
saying, "Can you track me
if I move five feet?"

00:02:02.722 --> 00:02:05.191 size:81% position:41%
And the Google C.E.O.
is perplexed and says,

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:07.060 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Well, it's Apple
that makes the iPhone."

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:10.697
So, you know, this doesn't
exactly inspire confidence

00:02:10.697 --> 00:02:15.235
given that we're the body
that has to regulate technology.

00:02:15.235 --> 00:02:17.237 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Again, you represent
Silicon Valley.

00:02:17.237 --> 00:02:20.907
You are also a co-chair of
Bernie Sanders' campaign.

00:02:20.907 --> 00:02:21.341 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I am.

00:02:21.341 --> 00:02:23.810
-So, obviously, that's a ver
progressive wing of the party.

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:27.313 align:start size:94% position:6%
You don't believe in this idea
of breaking up big tech.

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:29.949 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you do think
it requires reform?

00:02:29.949 --> 00:02:32.719 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is that the right word to use?
-Absolutely.

00:02:32.719 --> 00:02:33.386 size:88% position:44% line:92%
I mean, here's the deal.

00:02:33.386 --> 00:02:36.990
We're going through a technology
revolution in this country

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:37.824 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Everyone uses Google.

00:02:37.824 --> 00:02:39.425 align:start size:94% position:6%
Everyone gets packages
in Amazon.

00:02:39.425 --> 00:02:42.762
But there's been a concentration
of wealth and jobs

00:02:42.762 --> 00:02:44.864 align:start size:94% position:6%
and economic opportunity
in Silicon Valley.

00:02:44.864 --> 00:02:46.733 align:start size:94% position:6%
The challenge I really believe
of our time

00:02:46.733 --> 00:02:48.902 align:start size:94% position:6%
is how do we extend
the technology revolution

00:02:48.902 --> 00:02:52.939
to rural America, to minorit
communities, to places left out.

00:02:52.939 --> 00:02:55.441 size:78% position:39%
No one should have to
leave their hometown

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:57.644 align:start size:94% position:6%
just to get a job
in the 21st century.

00:02:57.644 --> 00:02:59.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, this is an interestin
situation for you

00:02:59.646 --> 00:03:02.916 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I think it's very rare
for someone who represents

00:03:02.916 --> 00:03:03.983 line:92%
the district basically sayin

00:03:03.983 --> 00:03:07.187 size:75% position:38%
not that you want to
collect the power,

00:03:07.187 --> 00:03:10.256 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you're basically admitting
there is too much power

00:03:10.256 --> 00:03:11.257 line:92%
right now in your district

00:03:11.257 --> 00:03:13.026 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There's too much
a concentration

00:03:13.026 --> 00:03:13.760 size:78% position:39% line:92%
of economic activity.

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:14.894 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm probably
the only Congressman

00:03:14.894 --> 00:03:17.564 align:start size:94% position:6%
where people are saying, "Look
there's too much traffic.

00:03:17.564 --> 00:03:18.698 align:start size:94% position:6%
The cost of housing
is too much."

00:03:18.698 --> 00:03:22.402
You know the average job a
a software company is 15 months?

00:03:22.402 --> 00:03:24.537 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, how long have you been
doing this?

00:03:24.537 --> 00:03:25.638 line:92%
I imagine more than 15 months.

00:03:25.638 --> 00:03:27.507 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, a lot longer than
15 months.

00:03:27.507 --> 00:03:28.341 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-So think about it.

00:03:28.341 --> 00:03:29.042 size:81% position:41% line:92%
People want to work --

00:03:29.042 --> 00:03:30.710
If you want to work five,
six, seven years somewhere

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:34.614
a Silicon Valley company shoul
go elsewhere as well to recruit.

00:03:34.614 --> 00:03:35.348 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And it's a win-win.

00:03:35.348 --> 00:03:36.316 line:92%
It's a win for my district

00:03:36.316 --> 00:03:37.684 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it'll be a win
for the country.

00:03:37.684 --> 00:03:39.953 align:start size:94% position:6%
Look, Donald Trump went around
the country

00:03:39.953 --> 00:03:40.653 size:81% position:41% line:92%
and he basically said,

00:03:40.653 --> 00:03:42.155 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I'm gonna bring
your old jobs back."

00:03:42.155 --> 00:03:42.622 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Right.

00:03:42.622 --> 00:03:45.558 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And the past is
better than the future.

00:03:45.558 --> 00:03:48.494 align:start size:94% position:6%
We've got to convince people
that technology is gonna

00:03:48.494 --> 00:03:51.631
bring new jobs, more opportunity
for their kids.

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:52.732 line:92%
And that the future is bette

00:03:52.732 --> 00:03:56.035 align:start size:94% position:6%
and something that they're
going to have access to

00:03:56.035 --> 00:03:56.803 size:84% position:42% line:92%
and the American dream.

00:03:56.803 --> 00:04:00.240 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There are, obviously,
a lot of elected officials

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:01.674 size:84% position:42% line:92%
because we have such --

00:04:01.674 --> 00:04:05.278 align:start size:94% position:6%
there is such a big field of
Democratic candidates

00:04:05.278 --> 00:04:06.145 line:92%
who haven't jumped in yet.

00:04:06.145 --> 00:04:09.115 align:start size:94% position:6%
You jumped in early as a
co-chair for Bernie's campaign

00:04:09.115 --> 00:04:12.785
What can you tell us about
Bernie that we might not kno

00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:14.988 line:92%
from seeing him in public?

00:04:14.988 --> 00:04:16.589 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He's got
a great sense of humor.

00:04:16.589 --> 00:04:18.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'll tell you
one quick anecdote.

00:04:18.591 --> 00:04:19.592 line:92%
-Because he seems very gruff

00:04:19.592 --> 00:04:22.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
There are times where he maybe
doesn't seem like

00:04:22.262 --> 00:04:23.263 line:92%
he has a great sense of humor.

00:04:23.263 --> 00:04:25.632 size:84% position:42%
-I mean, he's not quite
your sense of humor.

00:04:25.632 --> 00:04:28.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, thank you.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:28.368 --> 00:04:30.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But he's got
a dry sense of humor.

00:04:30.103 --> 00:04:32.672
I'll tell you, you know,
when he was hospitalized,

00:04:32.672 --> 00:04:35.642 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was going to be
speaking in Iowa for him.

00:04:35.642 --> 00:04:38.878 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so I asked the staff,
"What should I tell people?"

00:04:38.878 --> 00:04:40.413 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they said,
"Well, you tell them

00:04:40.413 --> 00:04:43.283 align:start size:94% position:6%
that he had
a myocardial infraction."

00:04:43.283 --> 00:04:46.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So instead of heart attack.
-Myocardial infraction.

00:04:46.185 --> 00:04:49.922
And so I'm just Googling this --
What is a myocardial infraction?

00:04:49.922 --> 00:04:51.924 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then I get
a call from Bernie Sanders

00:04:51.924 --> 00:04:53.793 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said, "Senator,
how are you doing?"

00:04:53.793 --> 00:04:54.961 line:92%
He says, "Oh, I'm doing great.

00:04:54.961 --> 00:04:56.796 align:start size:94% position:6%
He said,
"Ro, I don't recommend thoug

00:04:56.796 --> 00:04:58.031 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you ever get
a heart attack."

00:04:58.031 --> 00:05:00.833
So I said, "Alright, we're going
with heart attack."

00:05:00.833 --> 00:05:01.934 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:02.635 size:78% position:39% line:92%
And I'm glad you did.

00:05:02.635 --> 00:05:05.038
I think for the straight talk of
somebody like Bernie Sanders

00:05:05.038 --> 00:05:07.373 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's better
than myocardial infraction

00:05:07.373 --> 00:05:09.242 line:92%
-He's blunt. He's honest.

00:05:09.242 --> 00:05:12.912
But the main reason I'm backin
him is his platform is simple.

00:05:12.912 --> 00:05:14.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
He wants everyone
to have healthcare.

00:05:14.681 --> 00:05:16.549 align:start size:94% position:6%
He wants everyone
to have free education.

00:05:16.549 --> 00:05:19.018
You know, one of the worst
attacks when people say,

00:05:19.018 --> 00:05:21.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, giving Medicare for all
is elitist."

00:05:21.254 --> 00:05:22.188 align:start size:94% position:6%
Have you heard this?
-Yeah.

00:05:22.188 --> 00:05:26.859
-I mean, the idea -- when 66% of
Americans want Medicare for all,

00:05:26.859 --> 00:05:30.063
and if you're saying, "Look,
you're gonna get healthcare.

00:05:30.063 --> 00:05:31.431 line:92%
You don't have to pay co-pays.

00:05:31.431 --> 00:05:32.799 line:92%
You don't have to pay premiums

00:05:32.799 --> 00:05:34.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
You don't have to
pay deductibles."

00:05:34.233 --> 00:05:36.636 align:start size:94% position:6%
There are a lot of criticism
you could make.

00:05:36.636 --> 00:05:38.071 align:start size:94% position:6%
Elitist isn't one of them.
-Yeah.

00:05:38.071 --> 00:05:41.174
Well, best of luck with
everything going forward.

00:05:41.174 --> 00:05:43.343 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you so much
for making time for us tonight

00:05:43.343 --> 00:05:43.843 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Thank you.

00:05:43.843 --> 00:05:46.245 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Representative Ro Khanna,
everybody.

